From 5e45155c48c95584a32bc9009f71ba1e6a982145 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:39:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Upkeep U1: settable RTC clock (UPKEEP_PLAN U1)

The MC146818 clock stops being a read-only function of the
2026 power-on anchor.  Absolute time is now base_sec (Unix
seconds, 2026-01-01 at init) under the unchanged virtual tick
count, so dates before the anchor are representable and the
UIP/periodic phases do not move.

Register B gains its datasheet semantics (measured against
QEMU's mc146818rtc): the SET rising edge seeds the date bytes
from the live clock in the current format and clears UIE;
writes stage in those bytes and read back verbatim while SET;
the falling edge parses them under the format that was live
during SET, validates the civil ranges, and commits
base_sec, keeping the sub-second phase.  Invalid fields log
and change nothing.  The DM (BCD/binary) and 12/24-hour bits
now govern date reads and writes in both directions.  While
SET, UIP reads 0 and no update-ended flag is raised; the
periodic chain keeps running.

machine_t grows by the 8-byte base_sec, so pre-U1 snapshots
are refused by the existing header layout check rather than
reinterpreted (recorded in the plan and changelog).

Vectors (tests/test_rtc.c, 4 new groups): a leap-day set to
2024-02-29 with rollover and a warm reset preserving it;
SET freeze (staged reads, no UIP/UF) and an invalid month
leaving the clock untouched; binary-mode and 12-hour
round-trips including midnight/noon; SET clearing UIE.  All
pre-U1 vectors pass unmodified.  NC: rtc.c/rtc.h at U0 --
behavioural abort at the first staged-readback assert.
Gates: make test + test-sanitize green; both SeaBIOS ISO
lanes green for real (bios.bin + NASM present).
